# Staged runtime (copied from the PoB2 checkout) and generated artefacts.
runtime/
SimpleGraphic/Screenshots/
assets/fonts/*.ttf
tools/cache/

# Market MCP: public API responses (poe.ninja, poe2scout, trade site) cached for a few
# minutes so repeated questions do not hammer the endpoints. Never worth committing.
mcp-market/.cache/

# Market MCP: the working list (что взял в работу, по какой цене продал) - personal state.
mcp-market/.state/

# Build output. It used to be committed, which put 367 binaries in the tree (the Avalonia stack among
# them) and made every build show up as a change; the sources are the thing worth keeping.
bin/
obj/

# The panel's runtime scratch: the protocol files passed between the panel and the engine, the last
# capture, the engine's error log and the overlay's own log. All of it is rewritten on every run.
src/*.flag
src/last_item.txt
src/last_advice.txt
src/headless_error.txt
src/headless_request.lua
src/mcp_serve_*
src/mcp_request.lua
src/mcp_response.json
src/mcp_response.probe.json
src/probe_*.txt
src/probe_hold.txt
src/prefs.lua
src/session.log
src/boot_error.txt
src/capture_source.txt
src/captured_at.txt
src/ocr_item.txt
src/runtime_error.txt
src/test_results.txt
src/test_trace.txt
# The step loop's memory of the last item, and the coach's diagnostic dump. Both are rewritten on every
# capture and every test run, so tracking them left the tree permanently dirty - and a commit could carry
# one player's item state into the repository. The engine treats a missing file as "no memory of a previous
# step", so neither has to exist for anything to work.
src/craft_memory.lua
src/coach_diag.txt
*.log
